          "after": "Yellow 7/13/26: The City continues to experience delays in completing key project activities and has struggled to maintain project momentum, resulting in repeated discussions and extended decision-making timelines. A new City Project Manager has been assigned and will work alongside third-party PM Barry Dunn to improve coordination and accountability. The City is currently working with the Executive Steering Committee to revise the existing project management structure, recognizing that the current operating model is not effectively supporting project progress. Configuration completion is now targeted for July 20, which would enable the transition into formal system testing. However, schedule risk remains elevated as the City is reconsidering data conversion after previously selecting an archive-only approach. If conversion is pursued, significant timeline impacts are anticipated due to the delayed start. The project team is awaiting the City\u2019s internal decision and expects additional direction later this month."
